      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:458a00c6b5320bdb502e772eafd65caf8f6cccebb196a5f60180f06f88c45f28\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:3bbda5ce94978c6db1bc836f6a83b04e11879d632e8313f84eb1183c7c217fc3\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:5cf2ed46aac1d41602585d207154c6c52c1f29e6b7130c69d338510cad0b104d\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:380dc6728b6a9c348ff4af8705ac1c7f2134c2071a678bfbbae03b1a32efea44\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[\"d. The applicant's name is an integral part of her/his identity. Consequently, under 22 CFR 51.23(c), evidence of identity might be required in accordance with Department guidance to establish the name that best identifies the applicant:\"],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":2103,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":2103,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:1672:2103:sha256-a80eb4e1eddec9403c4f40ecea1e696a4799a061f2feeb00af71ab33871dd26a\",\"quote\":\"(1) If the applicant has had a material name change more than one year prior to applying on form DS-11 but has not updated her/his ID to reflect the material name change, you must suspend the application to request an acceptable ID in the new name. If there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name;\",\"start\":1672},{\"end\":2070,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:2067:2070:sha256-ee4d988c65de860fabbfbcd27f73d50bbebe3fba37fe419284f4811389c30bdc\",\"quote\":\"may\",\"start\":2067},{\"end\":2103,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:1672:2103:sha256-a80eb4e1eddec9403c4f40ecea1e696a4799a061f2feeb00af71ab33871dd26a\",\"quote\":\"(1) If the applicant has had a material name change more than one year prior to applying on form DS-11 but has not updated her/his ID to reflect the material name change, you must suspend the application to request an acceptable ID in the new name. If there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name;\",\"start\":1672},{\"end\":1670,\"field\":\"context:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:1433:1670:sha256-7fb835ed90fc315e25a5a9fafb4fd8b0f920d83c8e64fd1e2aa3da14a15e5930\",\"quote\":\"d. The applicant's name is an integral part of her/his identity. Consequently, under 22 CFR 51.23(c), evidence of identity might be required in accordance with Department guidance to establish the name that best identifies the applicant:\",\"start\":1433}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:24e58d7dd1b7b85ddfe34ac7a1633d5373b3bc48f628d3557edb3fabc8505f09\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"permission\",\"logic_text\":\"\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:380dc6728b6a9c348ff4af8705ac1c7f2134c2071a678bfbbae03b1a32efea44\",\"modality\":\"may\",\"modality_quote\":\"may\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:9f29adb47a49e803c37282f1e95e2c7f9b2f83a1d5c2632dc1b75424cd170269\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(1) If the applicant has had a material name change more than one year prior to applying on form DS-11 but has not updated her/his ID to reflect the material name change, you must suspend the application to request an acceptable ID in the new name. If there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name;\",\"references\":[\"form DS-11\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:ff8b55663ada12a8df50e3fcc7acf450991cd053ca01c0c144037105f1f2cb00\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(1) If the applicant has had a material name change more than one year prior to applying on form DS-11 but has not updated her/his ID to reflect the material name change, you must suspend the application to request an acceptable ID in the new name. If there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name;\"],\"scope_text\":\"If the applicant has had a material name change more than one year prior to applying on form DS-11 but has not updated her/his ID to reflect the material name change, and there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel.\",\"section_id\":\"fam-names-section-4\",\"start\":1672,\"summary\":\"If the applicant had a material name change more than one year prior to applying on form DS-11 without updating her/his ID and there is insufficient time to request that the applicant submit acceptable ID prior to urgent or emergency travel, a limited-validity passport may be issued in the requested name.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
